            <li>What would we pay to avoid this risk?</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Page 16: Ethics, Tensions & Debate -->
    <section>
      <div class="content-card-grid">
        <div class="content-card" style="grid-column: 1 / -1;">
          <h2>Ethics, Tensions & Debate</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="content-card">
          <h3>Tension Identification</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>What two (or more) values, goals, or priorities are in conflict?</li>
            <li>Is this a genuine conflict or a false dilemma?</li>
            <li>What makes this tension feel unresolvable?</li>
            <li>Who are the stakeholders on each side?</li>
            <li>Is there a third option that avoids the tradeoff?</li>
            <li>Can you reframe the problem to dissolve the tension?</li>
            <li>Would someone from a different context see this as a tension at all?</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="content-card">
          <h3>Moral Dilemma Resolution</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Are the values genuinely in conflict, or is one a disguised preference?</li>
            <li>Which option produces the best overall outcome?</li>
            <li>Which option respects duties and rights regardless of outcome?</li>
            <li>What would a person of strong character do here?</li>
            <li>Which option best preserves relationships and responds to vulnerability?</li>
            <li>Which option could everyone affected reasonably accept?</li>
